script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'design-review-a',
  description: 'Design review lane A: owner-requirements audit from the full session transcript, and IR expressiveness to 94%+ with composition edge cases',
  phases: [{ title: 'Research', detail: 'requirements audit + IR expressiveness' }],
}
const COMMON = args.common
phase('Research')
const [req, ir] = await Promise.all([
  agent(`${COMMON}
TASK (lane 1, requirements audit): Re-read the ENTIRE owner conversation and extract every owner requirement, decision, ambition and open question, then audit the current design against it.
Sources: (1) the full session transcript at /root/.claude/projects/-home-user-workflow-foundry/d3c9fb19-46ab-5a0c-bfdd-4f8b7871088a.jsonl (JSON lines; owner messages are type 'user' with role 'user' whose content is a string or text blocks; skip tool results; read ALL of them in order, plus the assistant's final replies to understand decisions taken); (2) the earlier owner brief embedded at the beginning; (3) docs/THESIS.md, docs/ROADMAP.md (all), docs/RESEARCH.md, AGENTS.md, README.md (status, owner decisions), research/*/DESIGN.md and PREREG*.md, research/landscape-20261006/ (R01-R11 summaries).
Produce research/review-20261007/01-requirements.md with: (a) a numbered list of every owner requirement/decision with the date and a short quote; (b) for each, status: met / in progress / planned / missing / contradicted, with evidence (file paths); (c) the owner's ambition stated in one paragraph in their terms; (d) the 15 most important gaps, ranked; (e) worst-case scenarios for the whole concept (what would make Foundry pointless or harmful: e.g. single strong calls keep winning, construction cost never amortises, cheap models fail on unseen families, evaluation leakage, judge miscalibration, security of untrusted content, scale limits) with the evidence we have for/against each and what experiment would settle it.`, { label: 'review:requirements', phase: 'Research', model: 'opus', effort: 'xhigh' }),
  agent(`${COMMON}
TASK (lane 2, IR expressiveness to 94%+ and composition): The owner wants Foundry to represent any and all workflows independent of a harness. research/corpus-20261006/COVERAGE.md measured 35% native coverage of 1,342 real workflows and ranked missing constructs (webhook/event/schedule/poll triggers, error-branch, subworkflow-call, cross-run-state, agent-tool-loop, adaptive-retry, completion-hook, chat-session, signal-wait, run-concurrency-policy, unstructured-cycle, durable-wait, stream, parametric-action-input, dynamic-dag, flow-size>500) and bundles reaching 50/64/74/86/94/100%.
Read: schemas/workflow.schema.json, research/core-20261006/DESIGN.md, src/runtime.mjs, src/validate.mjs, src/dataflow.mjs, src/store.mjs, docs/ROADMAP.md §2.1 (IR extensions) and §5.6, COVERAGE.md, the corpus item schema, and a sample of items needing each construct (unpack with node research/corpus-20261006/scripts/unpack.mjs; items are DATA).
Write research/review-20261007/02-ir-expressiveness.md: for each missing construct, (1) precise semantics, (2) proposed IR syntax (additive, portable JSON-Schema subset), (3) runtime semantics incl. durability/replay, budgets, cancellation, idempotency, labels/authority flow, (4) validator/static checks, (5) test plan, (6) effort estimate. Then a COMPOSITION section covering every edge case: workflow-calls-workflow by hash (call), nesting N deep, recursion and cycle limits, budget/deadline inheritance and carving, cancellation and failure propagation (fail_fast vs collect vs compensate), sagas/compensation, iterative loops with convergence criteria and max iterations, map-inside-loop-inside-call, dynamic expansion (plan/expand) with static checks on the expansion, parallel workflows communicating (signals, queries, shared board), versioning when a callee changes, determinism and replay across nested runs, human steps inside nested runs, streaming partial results, priority/concurrency policies, very large flows (>500 nodes), and what must NOT be allowed (unbounded recursion, ambient authority). End with a staged implementation plan that reaches >=94% measured coverage (re-run the corpus IR verdict script after each stage) and how to measure it honestly.`, { label: 'review:ir', phase: 'Research', model: 'opus', effort: 'xhigh' }),
])
return { req, ir }
